# Drop 3 jpgs here before rendering.
#
# Required:
#   primary.jpg      — close-up FACE shot (the identity anchor)
#   alternate-1.jpg  — full-body shot, outfit 1
#   alternate-2.jpg  — full-body shot, outfit 2
#
# CRITICAL: the face shot MUST be a separate file from the full-body shots.
# Seedream uses whichever file is in `reference_image` to extract the
# face embedding — if you give it a full-body shot, face identity drifts
# between shots. See characters/fengge/lessons.md for the EP001 ID-drift
# incident that motivated this rule.
#
# Spec:
#   - Format: .jpg (NOT .png — Seedream is tuned for jpg)
#   - Size:   ≥ 50KB (lint check), 1:1 or 3:4 aspect ratio
#   - Pose:   neutral, no props, plain background, no text/watermarks
#   - Lighting: even, no dramatic shadows
#   - Outfit in face shot: should match `character.yaml.canonical.primary`
#     description (the IP's most-recognizable look)
#
# After dropping the jpgs:
#   1. Update `character.yaml` → `character.canonical.alternates` with
#      the actual filenames (the template ships with placeholder names).
#   2. Run `python3 validators/canonical_image_check.py characters/<name>/canonical`
#   3. Then run your first test episode.
